From 925784135c7c1564381baa32f947ebbfda4bc23e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Toma=C5=BE=20Vajngerl?= <tomaz.vajngerl@collabora.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 13:35:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sc: expect the optimal value of the knapsack fixture
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 15-item model has a unique optimum of 6987. The system lp_solve
finds that optimum, so use the value established by the upstream fix.

Backport the expected-value correction; keep this release's lp_solve
test engine. The upstream commit also removes the lp_solve component,
which is outside this correction.

Upstream-Commit: https://github.com/LibreOffice/core/commit/bfc9cfdecf54885bb0d38ad29fee36affd0d9df5
Signed-off-by: Tomaž Vajngerl <tomaz.vajngerl@collabora.co.uk>
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
 sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx b/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx
index b7735a7..e404dae 100644
--- a/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx
+++ b/sc/qa/extras/scsolverobj.cxx
@@ -116,8 +116,9 @@ void ScSolverSettingsObj::testXSolverSettings()
     xSolverModel->setSuppressDialog(true);
     xSolverModel->solve();
 
-    // The correct solution value is 6981 (using LpsolveSolver)
-    CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL(static_cast<double>(6981), xSheet->getCellByPosition(6, 6)->getValue());
+    // The optimal total value for this knapsack is 6987, which fills the weight
+    // capacity of 1000 exactly.
+    CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL(static_cast<double>(6987), xSheet->getCellByPosition(6, 6)->getValue());
 
     // Check objective function and variable cells
     testCellAddress(aObjCell, xSolverModel->getObjectiveCell());
-- 
2.54.0

